It also makes sense in the general pattern of Nethack.  Die and maybe
you retain some of your efforts maybe you don't.  When you arrive at
a bones level if it gets loaded you get all that stuff, and
inconveniently
enough you also get whatever killed that player.  Wonderfull for
learning
lessons.  Now what should I try *this* time since the frontal assault
failed the first time and the missile method failed the second time?
;^)

There's also the fact that the items tend to be level-appropriate thus
roughly doubling your amount of stuff once you've learned how to
easily handled curses.  Even better on a multi-player system it could
be from someone with a much more acquisitive playing style of a much
less acquisitive playing style so you could end up with someone else's
problems-not-stuff or stuff-not-problems.


